# First-class product parity

`@qvac/cli` (`qvac serve`, `qvac configure`) is a first-class SDK product. Exposing an addon feature on the SDK is not done at the plugin + client API.

## Same PR

A user-facing inference change (new modality, new request/sampling field, new load-time `modelConfig` field) includes CLI in **this** PR, or the PR body says it is library-only and why.

Native addon PRs stay native. Do not mix C++/prebuilds into the CLI PR. The follow-up SDK exposure PR is where CLI belongs.

## What to update

| Change | CLI in the same PR |
|---|---|
| HTTP-visible request/sampling field | `packages/cli/src/serve/schemas` (e.g. `extractGenerationParams`), test, HTTP docs |
| Load-time `modelConfig` field | `packages/cli/src/configure/param-schemas.ts` `SCHEMA_BY_ADDON` when that addon is in configure; serve config mapping if `serve.models` loads it |
| New first-class modality | HTTP route (QVAC extension if no OpenAI URL), CLI test, HTTP docs, or an explicit library-only note |

Do **not** put `invokePlugin`, P2P provide, KV-cache admin, or suspend/resume on HTTP unless they are already a serve product.

## Agents

CLI is in scope for SDK exposure tasks unless the task says library-only. A missing CLI diff with no opt-out is a gap, not a follow-up.
